E
"corpses aftermath"
"By the look of the corpses, the Unity army came away with a victory here. 
Nine of the twelve corpses are creatures from the Mephistophelian army.  Two
goblins, two wolves, four orcish axemen, and one currently armless ogre make
up the deceased of the evil race.  A dwarf and two humans are the good race
casualties.
"
E
"2 ogre"
"This ogre appears to have been de-armed in combat, although a human finger
poking out of its mouth would have you believe it wasn't without cost. 
Something shiny glints from under the massive corpse's torso.
"
E
"orcish"
"The orcish axemen were probably surrounded when they gave in, as sword and axe
marks on their chest and back attest.  One of the orcs, bigger than the
others, seems to have accounted for two of the three Unity deaths, as their
bodies are stacked almost on top of each other.
"
E
"goblins"
"These goblin wolfriders died with snarls on their face, but their unbloodied
spears show the impotence of their death.
"
E
"wolf wolves"
"Two wolves lie here, killed by some kind of piercing weapon, their goblish
saddles still buckled tightly on.
"
E
"humans"
"Two human warriors lie under the corpse of a unusually large orc, the larger
one still grasping the sword that pierced the foul creature's heart.  The
humans were armed with swords and shields, and bear seal of Chiiron on their
helmets.
"
E
"dwarf dwarven"
"The head of this dead dwarven warrior was crushed by some tremendous blunt
weapon, most likely the club wielded by the Ogre.  He has the symbol of Kha-Da
blazoned on his breastplate, and still holds a bloody axe tightly in both
hands.
"
E
"weapons"
"A club, a sword, five axes, and two spears are littered on the ground, bent
and broken.  None of them look to be in usable condition.
"
