E
"chunks rock beams wood"
"Chunks of rock, both large and small, are piled high to the east.  The white
granite remains are littered with broken and torn planks of wood, and a single
unbroken beam of wood leans up against the pile, its other end planted firmly
into the riverbed.
"
E
"water pool weeds leaves"
"The brackish water is composed of leave, weeds, mud, and various dead
insects.  A faint, but foul odor arises from the unpleasant mixture.  Even
though the water is only a foot deep, the filth conceals the river's bottom.
"
E
"bank"
"The bank here has slid into the water, changing the climb from a vertical
effort to a fourty-five degree scramble.  The mud is quite sticky, but
tentative testing reveals that it is relatively firm after a half-foot of
sinking into it.
"
E
"mud"
"The muck here is primarily dark brown with traces of crimson, the occasionl
bits of foliage or rock attempting to distguish itself from the mud's uniform
color and texture.
"
