E
"swaths grass"
"Looking closely at these swaths of grass reveal bits and pieces of wood, all
of the same type, pressed in among the grass.  You also notice that the swaths
begin here, pointing toward the bridge, then seem to curve and disappear into
the mud to the west.
"
E
"bridge supports"
"The bridge seems to have been shattered by a massive boulder, which can barely
be seen poking out of the middle of the river below.  Crumbled bits of rock
lie scattered among more of the sizable remains of the stone supports that
once held this bridge up, totally covering the bank and making it unclimbable.
"
E
"wooden logs"
"This wall of linked logs is made in the spirit of a log cabin, except twice as
tall.  A full twenty feet it rises, protecting a watchtower filled ominously
with arrow slits.  The logs themselves are coated with an extremely slippery
substance that smells faintly of oil and fish, making them impossible to climb.
"
E
"watchtower"
"This wooden watchtower looks recently built, as the wood is hardly marred by
battle or weather.  There are a total of twelve arrow slits that you can see,
all pointing in this general direction.  You are too far away to see any more
detail.
"
-1
