E
"ground"
"Looking closely at the ground, you can see faint footprints that lead toward a
medium sized pine tree.
"
E
"trees"
"Behind the tree is a discarded quiver, probably left behind by an archer in a
hurry.  The quiver has the mark of Vaasa stitched into its leather.
"
E
"river water"
"The river here is only about four feet below the bank, looking cold an
uninviting.  You shudder at the thought of jumping in.
"
E
"wall logs"
"This wall of linked logs is made in the spirit of a log cabin, except twice as
tall.  A full twenty feet it rises, protecting a watchtower filled ominously
with arrow slits.  The logs themselves are coated with an extremely slippery
substance that smells faintly of oil and fish, making them impossible to climb.
"
E
"dam rock wood"
"In the distance, you see that a collapsed bridge is the cause of the dam.  The
rock and wood are its remains.
"
