#86006
"Shallows of a River"
"The river here is shallow, partially due to a high point in the riverbed and
partially to the debri from the destruction of the bridge to the east.  The
water is about three feet deep, flowing slowly west with a contented burble. 
To the north are shallows overlooked by an undamaged bank of mud and grass,
while to the south are shallows partially filled with mud by its collapsed
bank.
"
""
