"debri bridge"
"From here you have a good view of the giant boulder that smashed the bridge to
the east.  The boulder was probably near twenty feet high, although it's
difficult to tell as much of it is buried in the riverbed.  The remains of the
bridge seemed to be made of wood, but this view shows that it had iron
supports underneath it.
"
